<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Derawar Fort</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Derawar Fort is a large square fortress in the Cholistan Desert of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, south of Bahawalpur, whose forty massive bastions are visible from far across the desert. A fort was held there by Bhati <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajputs</a> before the Abbasi nawabs of Bahawalpur took it in 1733 and rebuilt it, and it remained in the possession of the nawabs' family.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/derawar-fort.jpg" alt="Derawar Fort" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fassifarooq · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Derawar_Fort,_Bahawalpur_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
